son\": \"There is no public code, so text and code cannot be compared.\"\n  },\n  \"S5_runs\": {\n    \"code\": \"10\",\n    \"quote\": \"Dataset A, Dataset B, Dataset C, are input into the neural network model, and the average of the results of 10 experiments is selected as the final result.\",\n    \"location\": \"p.6\",\n    \"reason\": \"The headline CWRU result is the mean of 10 runs. Table 4 lists the result of each of the 10 tests.\"\n  },\n  \"S5_spread_reported\": {\n    \"code\": \"Y\",\n    \"quote\": \"The results of each test for Dataset A, Dataset B, and Dataset C are shown in Table 4\",\n    \"location\": \"p.6\",\n    \"reason\": \"No standard deviation or interval is reported, but Table 4 lists all 10 individual run accuracies, so the spread is directly visible. That is more than reporting only the mean, so the closest code is Y. The comparison experiments, by contrast, report only means.\"\n  },\n  \"S6_metrics\": {\n    \"code\": \"M\",\n    \"quote\": \"Fig. 7. Fault classification results. (a) confusion matrix of Dataset A.\",\n    \"location\": \"p.7\",\n    \"reason\": \"Results are reported as accuracy plus confusion matrices (Fig. 7). I found no F1, precision or recall anywhere in the paper.\"\n  },\n  \"S7_noise_protocol\": {\n    \"code\": \"U\",\n    \"quote\": \"Gaussian white noise was added to the experimental data to simulate real noise.\",\n    \"location\": \"p.8\",\n    \"reason\": \"Sections 3.4–3.5 contain noise experiments at -4 to 4 dB. The paper only says the noise is added to the CWRU dataset or the experimental data. It does not say whether the training set, the test set, or both are noisy, so the protocol is unclear.\"\n  },\n  \"S8_traceability\": {\n    \"code\": \"0\",\n    \"quote\": \"The authors do not have permission to share data.\",\n    \"location\": \"p.12\",\n    \"reason\": \"The paper gives no link to code, weights, training logs or raw result files. The data availability statement says the data cannot be shar